  "summary": "OceanLotus (APT32) deployed its SPECTRALVIPER backdoor in two 2024-2026 Windows campaigns: a supply-chain compromise of the FireAnt MetaKit update server targeting Vietnamese stock investors, and a long-running intrusion into an infrastructure and transport construction corporation. SPECTRALVIPER is delivered via renamed signed side-loader executables (Toolbox.exe and dtlupdate.exe copies) with a -uiDll DLL side-load, then injects into a host process and beacons over HTTPS with encrypted host data in a Cookie header prefixed euconsent-v2= or zd_cs_pm=.",
